Gemma in Fabulous OS
====================

The assistant is Google's Gemma 4 model (the "E2B" size), run on this computer
by the open-source program llama.cpp. It needs no internet connection, and it
is started without any network access at all.

Model:   gemma-4-E2B_q4_0-it.gguf, from Google's own repository
         https://huggingface.co/google/gemma-4-E2B-it-qat-q4_0-gguf
         The exact revision and SHA-256 checksum are in models.lock in the
         Fabulous OS repository; the build refuses a file that does not match.
         Licence: Apache 2.0 (Gemma-LICENSE-Apache-2.0 in this folder).
Add-on:  gemma-4-E2B-it-mmproj.gguf, from the same repository of Google's,
         same licence. It lets Gemma look at pictures and listen to sound
         recordings that you attach. Looking at a picture can take minutes
         on a slow processor, and Gemma can misreport what it sees or hears.
Program: llama.cpp, MIT licence (llama.cpp-LICENSE-MIT and
         llama.cpp-VERSION in this folder).

Gemma can be wrong. Check anything important.
